{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "23", "m": "08", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "08", "M": "16", "S": "03"}}, "news": [{"title": "Ageing Delhi colonies to get a chance to rebuild, grow under master plan 2047", "para": "Delhi's Master Plan 2047 outlines a strategy to rejuvenate aging government colonies and housing societies. To initiate redevelopment, a minimum plot size of 3,000 square metres is necessary for any new construction. Residents have the option to combine properties for modernization, leading to improved living conditions and amenities. Additionally, any new road development must gain approval before projects can begin.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/ageing-delhi-colonies-to-get-a-chance-to-rebuild-grow-under-master-plan-2047/133419799?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-278324/133419799.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}, {"title": "Varanasi: 276 property owners pay over \u20b939 lakh in tax under OTS in three days", "para": "In just three days, the Varanasi Municipal Corporation's tax settlement initiative has successfully garnered \u20b939.36 lakh in property taxes. Taxpayers benefited from a considerable waiver of \u20b97.18 lakh on interest and surcharge fees. This program not only offers total waivers on these extra charges for lump-sum principal payments but also allows small and medium taxpayers to manage dues of up to \u20b91 lakh in three manageable monthly installments.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/varanasi-276-property-owners-pay-over-39-lakh-in-tax-under-ots-in-three-days/133419773?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-154352/133419773.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}, {"title": "Goa government gives more time to file applications to regularise homes on comunidade land", "para": "The Goa cabinet has decided to extend the application timeline for the regularization of homes built on comunidade land, increasing the deadline from six to eighteen months. This change will be formalized through the introduction of the Goa Legislative Diploma No. 2070 Amendment Bill, 2026. The initiative addresses encroachments by landless individuals prior to February 28, 2014, aiming to balance humanitarian needs and reclamation of comunidade land.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/goa-government-gives-more-time-to-file-applications-to-regularise-homes-on-comunidade-land/133419679?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-298820/133419679.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}]}